      "OracleCard": {
        "description": "A card aggregated across its printings, shaped by ``AGGREGATE_CARD``.\n\n``id`` is the oracle id the group was keyed on, and it is required. That\nis the one piece of strictness worth an outage: it is the value every\nclient builds a card URL from, and while it lived only in ``_expose_id``\nit was a convention rather than a contract. Declaring it required turns\na group with no oracle id - what a ``reversible_card`` layout produces,\nsince Scryfall puts the oracle id on each face instead of the card -\ninto a loud failure at the boundary instead of an empty ``href``.",
        "properties": {
          "card_count": {
            "title": "Card Count",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "card_text": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
